Figure 1: 
Example sightline through the simulation showing the impact of UVB fluctuations on the Ly$\alpha$ forest flux.
From top to bottom, the panels show:
(1) the matter overdensity, $\Delta$;
(2) the gas temperature, T;
(3) the normalized photoionization rate, $\Gamma/\langle\Gamma\rangle$, for four values of the mean free path, $\lambda_{\text{mfp}}$, 5, 10, 30, and 150 cMpc;
(4) the corresponding transmitted flux fraction along the same sightline; and
(5) the transmitted flux for the $\lambda_{\text{mfp}}=150$ cMpc model after forward modeling to a spectral resolution of $R=8800$ and a signal-to-noise ratio of $\mathrm{SNR}=30$. Also included in this panel is a dashed red line showing the $1\sigma$ noise level, $\sigma_{F}\simeq 0.033$ (see Equation (6)).
